1
00:00:00,967 --> 00:00:04,567
In this lesson, you'll add an enemy
that bounces around the screen.

2
00:00:04,907 --> 00:00:07,607
If it touches you, your
score goes back to zero.

3
00:00:08,067 --> 00:00:10,107
The player and the coin are folded up.

4
00:00:10,307 --> 00:00:12,627
Our new sprite is define sprite enemy.

5
00:00:12,933 --> 00:00:16,293
From Program, drag create
sprite under the coin's.

6
00:00:16,333 --> 00:00:19,033
Pick enemy, and put it
in a corner, at 300, 20.

7
00:00:22,567 --> 00:00:25,687
From Looks, look like a circle
goes into define sprite enemy.

8
00:00:26,107 --> 00:00:28,667
Make it a box, size 18, and red.

9
00:00:30,800 --> 00:00:32,600
Also from Looks, point in direction,

10
00:00:32,640 --> 00:00:34,700
with 40, to fly on a slant.

11
00:00:35,667 --> 00:00:37,687
Then forever: move forward 2 steps,

12
00:00:37,727 --> 00:00:39,147
and bounce off the edges.

13
00:00:46,967 --> 00:00:48,687
Inside the forever, an if,

14
00:00:48,727 --> 00:00:50,107
with touching sprite player.

15
00:00:58,800 --> 00:01:00,460
When it hits you, from Variables,

16
00:01:00,500 --> 00:01:02,960
set score to 0, and play sound hit.

17
00:01:08,100 --> 00:01:10,360
And from Motion, go to x 300,

18
00:01:10,400 --> 00:01:13,440
y 20, so the enemy starts
again from its corner.

19
00:01:14,600 --> 00:01:16,640
Press Run, click the game, and play.

20
00:01:17,033 --> 00:01:19,713
Catch the coins, and keep
away from the red box,

21
00:01:19,753 --> 00:01:21,333
or your score drops to zero.

22
00:01:22,633 --> 00:01:24,733
In the code, moving
forward became advance,

23
00:01:24,773 --> 00:01:26,993
and bounce became four IFs,

24
00:01:27,033 --> 00:01:28,693
one for each edge of the screen.

25
00:01:29,100 --> 00:01:29,780
Well done!

26
00:01:29,820 --> 00:01:31,500
In lesson five, it's free play:

27
00:01:31,660 --> 00:01:32,760
make your own game.
